  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Movements Trust regranter</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Movements Trust was founded in 2021 to act as a conduit to increase the funding to reach social movements.It acts as both a values driven fiscalsponsor and regranter for movements in the UK and in the global majorityworld, and aims to use regranting practice to demonstrate better ways to grant to social movements. One of itsfounders, Sarah Greenfield Clark remains involved in TMT&#x2019;s operations asa freelance associate and is leading thisproject.TMT comprises an active Board of 7 Trustees, include threefinance professionals, who set the strategy, overseeand conduct due diligence on movement applications, and monitor financial and governance responsibilitiesTMT is run by Executive Director, Anna Henry who is supported in addition to Sarah Greenfield Clark as chiefclimate movement builder, by a Movement Officer, and an Operational Manager who runs the financial andapplication systems. In TMT&#x2019;s first year, just under &#xa3;0.5M was distributed to movements; in 2023-24 we havealready exceeded this and forecast distributing at least &#xa3;0.6M.

Sarah Greenfield Clark attended the Camp and facilitated discussion with participants about the best use, focus andpurpose behind a grant fund to most effectively support the ideas and movements generated by the Camp. Shenowmaintains an active core of delegates as advisers who will work with TMT to oversee, assess and decide ondistribution of the grants in January 2024.In its grant making and sponsorship to date , TMT has developed robust due diligence processes, matched byastrong, values led and coproduction-based system of grant distribution and follow up, which prioritises movementsin grant making processes.TMT willsupport the core group and grant recipients to report back on progress, learning and plans at the nextCampin2024, in partnership with Greenpeace Roots, and will be developing a second pooled funds to distribute toCamp participants in 2024, building on learning from this year.</narrative>
  </description>
